# No perfect cuboid has two edges in ratio `420 : 851`

Generated by `scripts/cuboid_class_cert.py` (do not edit by hand):

```
python3 scripts/cuboid_class_cert.py --sq --parts 2 30,7
```

This is the fiber `(m, n) = (30, 7)`, with `U = 851`, `V = 420`, `W = 949`,
through the curve `E″` itself: moving a root to `0` makes it the pair curve of
`(p, q) = (U², V²) = (176400, 724201)` (sorted), with `D = q² − p² = 493350128401`,
and a cuboid on the fiber gives a solution with `M² ≠ pq e²`
(`IsPerfectCuboid.not_onFiber_of_sq`). Unlike the pair `(2UV, W²)`, this pair has the
solutions `M² = pq e²` of the point `T₄` of order `4`, so the descent shows only that every
solution is of this kind (`sq_eq_of_isSol_of_casesOKT`). It has 108000 groups
`(λ, σ₀)` over 1215 values of `λ`; 107870 of them are ruled out by their `2`-descent
class (`ClassKill`, with 625 distinct class tests), and the other 38684 cases are
split out, 26460 of them torsion translates and 64 of them by family TR (the
half-points of `±T₄` minus a point of order `8`, `trOK`). The kernel replays the certificate
with `classCert` (`decide +kernel`).

The curve `E″` has rank `0` and its `2`-Selmer group is its torsion modulo `2` (PARI/GP); this is
only the reason to expect the descent to work, and the proofs do not depend on it.

## Main results

* `Descent.sq_eq_thirty_seven` — the descent for the pair `(176400, 724201)`.
* `not_isPerfectCuboid_420_851` — no perfect cuboid has `851 X = 420 Z`.
-/

